From 2a89928fea690c1e2bcff1db89de7aab54985879 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:02:19 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): a pinned route's quota wall hit at agent build
 shows its reset and Choose a model [daveey]

A chat pinned to a quota-walled subscription route (anthropic/claude-fable-5-2, example Desktop incident) failed
at agent BUILD time with SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable. The user got a toast with the raw epoch reset and
`hermes setup` advice, an agent_init_failed "Couldn't start this chat ... Retry" card, and a "Send it again"
boundary. The pre-build refusal of the same pin (#2516) already reads as a route_refused card with the reset
in PT and /model; the build-time path now matches it.

- agent/model_routing_walls.py: walled_pin_reply(provider, model, resets_at) factored out of held_reply
  (text unchanged).
- agent/model_routing_unavailable.py: quota_refusal_wall(exc) -> (provider, model, resets_at) when the
  terminal quota refusal names its route and carries a finite absolute reset.
- tui_gateway/user_messages.py: agent_init_failed_message returns walled_pin_reply for such a build failure;
  route_refused gets its own turn-error title/hint (not the gateway layer's "internal error ... /retry").
- tui_gateway/session_registry.py: the build-failure handler records agent_failure.failure_route
  {provider, model, resets_at}; credential_failure.client_failure_fields drops it like failure_resets_at,
  so no client frame or RPC error data carries it.
- tui_gateway/methods_prompt.py: _run_after_agent_ready closes a turn whose build hit that wall with
  {layer: gateway, code: route_refused, retryable: false, message: <walled reply>} and the
  ROUTE_REFUSED_TURN_NOTICE boundary; every other build failure keeps agent_init_failed / FAILED_TURN_NOTICE.
  session_failure_payload still folds reset_at into that route_refused frame.

Tests (RED on the source-only revert, GREEN after): tests/tui_gateway/test_agent_init_quota_wall_card.py
(message, fallback chain, controls; failure_route recorded and absent from the strict-contract error event
and _wait_agent data; turn frame surface + boundary row; agent_init_failed control). Desktop:
route-refused-completion.test.tsx gains the agent_init-path frame (contract check; Desktop code unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
